{#- SPEC-hm-light-lane-s2b ADR-003: the one pointer every stage command uses to send the main loop to a
    reference file under `.claude/hm/`. Callers set `ref_file`, `ref_use` and (optionally) `ref_stop`
    before the include. One physical line, because a pointer that wraps is read as two. The file is
    read from the project root, never `<WT>`: a worktree copy can be stale (SPEC-hm-light-lane-s2 S3).
    With worktree isolation off there is no `<WT>` to name, so the pointer says "a worktree" (the
    worktree-off renders carry no `<WT>` at all). -#}
{% set ptr_wt = config.worktree is defined and config.worktree.get('enabled') -%}
Read `.claude/hm/{{ ref_file }}` from the project root (above `.worktrees/`), never from {{ '`<WT>`' if ptr_wt else 'a worktree' }}, {{ ref_use }}. If it is missing or unreadable, name `{{ ref_file }}`, say to re-render with `/hm:make`, and STOP{{ ref_stop | default('') }}.
